-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice2-fixes.prompt.md\\\\\\\\n?? collab/1790479176072-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice2-confirm.gpt-6-sol.findings.md\\\\\\\\n?? collab/1790479176072-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice2-confirm.gpt-6-sol.prompt.md\\\\\\\\n?? collab/1790479176072-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice2-confirm.gpt-6-sol.stdout.log\\\\\\\\n?? collab/1790479180000-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice2-fixes-r2.glm-flash.report.md\\\\\\\\n?? collab/1790479180000-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice2-fixes-r2.prompt.md\\\\\\\\n?? collab/1790481481207-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice2-confirm-r2.gpt-6-sol.prompt.md\\\\\\\\n?? collab/1790481481207-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice2-confirm-r2.gpt-6-sol.stdout.log\\\\\\\\n?? public/chp/blog/muse-ai-agent-on-datom-world.blog\\\\\\\\n?? src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc\\\\\\\\n?? test/dao/stream/remote_test.cljc\\\\\\\\n./test/dao/data/btree_async_test.cljc:94:(defn- drain!\\\\\\\\n./collab/1790479180000-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice2-fixes-r2.glm-flash.report.md:4:- `remote.cljc:281-300` — `send-request!`: on `:dao.stream/ok` it registers outstanding (registered-sends-only preserved) and clears the id from `:pending`; on a `:dao.stream/full` refusal of a descriptor probe it keeps the request in `:pending` instead of dropping it. Cursor/next/append! full refusals still leave nothing outstanding and nothing pending, exactly as in fix round 1.\\\\\\\\n./collab/1790479180000-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice2-fixes-r2.glm-flash.report.md:5:- `remote.cljc:458-464` — new `retry-pending!`: one more try of each kept probe per call.\\\\\\\\n./collab/1790479180000-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice2-fixes-r2.glm-flash.report.md:6:- `remote.cljc:467-481` — `drain!` calls `retry-pending!` once per drain (same cadence as the outstanding-probe ask counting), so after writer recovery the kept probe is re-sent; on acceptance it becomes the outstanding probe and the normal filing path (`absorb!` → `learn!`/`emit!`) confirms it.\\\\\\\\n./collab/1790479180000-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice2-fixes-r2.glm-flash.report.md:7:- `remote.cljc:659-678` — `refl-close` also forgets this reflection's kept probe, so nothing crosses for a closed reflection (preserving round-1 close semantics).\\\\\\\\n./collab/1790479180000-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice2-fixes-r2.glm-flash.report.md:10:- New gate test `a-refused-probe-is-kept-and-retried-on-a-later-drain` (:616): attach through a writer refusing 2 sends — the probe is refused and kept; the first drain's one retry is refused too (0 descriptor requests on the wire, no event); a later drain retries once and it crosses (= 1, proving once-per-drain); after one `serve!` the answer is filed the normal way (confirmation event with identity, ok, surface #{:reader}) and the learned surface answers `append!` as no-surface locally with nothing crossing.\\\\\\\\n./collab/1790479176072-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice2-confirm.gpt-6-sol.stdout.log:14:{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item_5\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc | sed -n '1,620p'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"     1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(ns dao.stream.remote\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"DaoStream remote: any stream, reachable as itself\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     3\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   (docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md, sections 2 through 2.5).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     4\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     5\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   A peer that holds a handle answers the handle's own operations as\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     6\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   data over a channel; a peer at the other end holds a handle -- the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     7\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   reflection -- whose operations are those questions asked across the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     8\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   channel, with the source's outcome maps returned verbatim.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     9\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    10\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   `mirror-step` is the pure answering step a peer runs over a channel\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    11\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   against its table. It never constructs, parses or rewrites a cursor,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    12\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   an anchor or an outcome, and its steps 1 to 4 are its only contacts\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    13\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   with the entry's handle: every cursor, next and append! runs through\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    14\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   `dao.stream.middleware/apply-request` with the channel context, so\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    15\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   nothing bypasses the entry's middleware or its declared surface.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    16\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   `attacher` is the composition's :dao.stream/attach entry for\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    17\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   :dao.stream/remote descriptors; it keeps one link per channel\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    18\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   descriptor, shared by every reflection through that channel, and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    19\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   answers ok at once -- the contract's deferred remote confirmation.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    20\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   There is no :dao.stream/create entry: attaching through this\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    21\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   transport never creates.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    22\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    23\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            [dao.stream.middleware :as middleware]))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    24\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    25\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    26\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    27\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t;; Wire shapes (2.1)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    28\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    29\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    30\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(def ^:private wire-ops\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    31\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The four wire operations. close! never crosses -- the mirror holds\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    32\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   nothing per remote party to close and the owner's close is never\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    33\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   remote -- and attach! never crosses, because it consumes a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    34\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   descriptor and produces a local handle.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    35\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  #{:dao.stream/descriptor :dao.stream/cursor :dao.stream/next\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    36\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    :dao.stream/append!})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    37\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    38\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    39\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(def ^:private protocol-errors\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    40\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The three protocol errors, one answer shape for every operation,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    41\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   a key instead of an outcome map because no operation's outcome set\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    42\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   can carry them.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    43\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  #{:dao.stream.remote/not-found\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    44\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    :dao.stream.remote/no-surface\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    45\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    :dao.stream.remote/oversize})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    46\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    47\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    48\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- well-formed-request?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    49\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"True when `v` is a well-formed request: a map naming its identity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    50\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   and one of the four wire ops, carrying an args vector and the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    51\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   asker-minted id. Anything else is dropped as malformed wire input.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    52\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [v]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    53\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (and (map? v)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    54\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t       (contains? v :dao.stream/identity)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    55\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t       (contains? wire-ops (:dao.stream.remote/op v))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    56\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t       (vector? (:dao.stream.remote/args v))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    57\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t       (contains? v :dao.stream.remote/id)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    58\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    59\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    60\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- well-formed-answer?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    61\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"True when `v` is a well-formed answer: a map carrying the id and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    62\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   the identity and either a protocol error or an outcome map.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    63\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [v]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    64\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (and (map? v)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    65\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t       (contains? v :dao.stream.remote/id)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    66\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t       (contains? v :dao.stream/identity)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    67\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t       (or (contains? protocol-errors (:dao.stream.remote/error v))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    68\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t           (stream/outcome-map? v))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    69\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    70\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    71\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- required-surface\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    72\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The declared surface `op` needs, under the fixed mapping: cursor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    73\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   and next need :reader, append! needs :writer, descriptor needs no\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    74\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   surface and is always answerable.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    75\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [op]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    76\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (case op\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    77\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (:dao.stream/cursor :dao.stream/next) :reader\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    78\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    :dao.stream/append! :writer\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    79\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    nil))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    80\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    81\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    82\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- error-answer\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    83\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The protocol-error answer shape, with the id and identity the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    84\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   request carried.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    85\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [identity id e]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    86\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  {:dao.stream/identity identity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    87\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   :dao.stream.remote/id id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    88\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   :dao.stream.remote/error e})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    89\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    90\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    91\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    92\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t;; The mirror step (2.3)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    93\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    94\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    95\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- valid-budget?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    96\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"True when the request carries the optional next-only budget as a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    97\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   positive integer. Anything else ignores the budget, which is always\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    98\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   correct for a mirror.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    99\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [req]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   100\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (let [k (:dao.stream.remote/budget req)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   101\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (and (integer? k) (pos? k))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   102\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   103\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   104\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- chase\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   105\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The budget chase: `outcome` is an ok from next; follow the successor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   106\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   cursor through the same apply-request path at most k - 1 further\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   107\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   times, collecting the further outcome maps in order. The vector ends\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   108\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   at and includes the first non-ok outcome, so blocked, end and gap\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   109\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   reach the reader with the source's own recovery cursor.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   110\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [h ctx k outcome]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   111\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (loop [more [] cur (:dao.stream/cursor outcome) n 1]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   112\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (if (or (>= n k) (nil? cur))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   113\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      more\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   114\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (let [r (middleware/apply-request h ctx\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   115\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                        {:dao.stream.remote/op\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   116\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                         :dao.stream/next\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   117\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                         :dao.stream.remote/args [cur]})]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   118\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t        (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   119\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (recur (conj more r) (:dao.stream/cursor r) (inc n))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   120\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (conj more r))))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   121\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   122\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   123\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- write-answer!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   124\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Append one answer value toward the asker. A value the channel cannot\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   125\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   carry (invalid-value) is answered with the oversize protocol error\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   126\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   in place of that element, the read not skipped and no cursor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   127\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   advanced past it; any other refused write leaves the request\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   128\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   unanswered.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   129\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [chan-writer answer]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   130\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (let [r (stream/append! chan-writer answer)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   131\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (when (= :dao.stream/invalid-value (:dao.stream/outcome r))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   132\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (stream/append! chan-writer\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   133\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                      (error-answer (:dao.stream/identity answer)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   134\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                    (:dao.stream.remote/id answer)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   135\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                    :dao.stream.remote/oversize)))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   136\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   137\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   138\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- answer!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   139\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The mirror's steps 1 to 4 for one well-formed request: look the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   140\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   identity up in the table (not-found); check the op against the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   141\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   entry's declared surface under the fixed mapping (no-surface);\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   142\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   answer descriptor from the entry's handle directly, adding the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   143\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   declared surface, and apply cursor, next and append! through\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   144\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   apply-request with the channel context; append the answer with the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   145\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   id and identity. For next with a budget k, and an ok first outcome,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   146\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   the chase places the further outcomes under more.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   147\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [table chan-writer channel req]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   148\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (let [identity (:dao.stream/identity req)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   149\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t        id (:dao.stream.remote/id req)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   150\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t        op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   151\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t        entry (get table identity)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   152\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (if-not entry\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   153\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (write-answer! chan-writer\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   154\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                     (error-answer identity id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   155\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                   :dao.stream.remote/not-found))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   156\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (let [h (:handle entry)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   157\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t        (if (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   158\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (write-answer!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   159\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            chan-writer\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   160\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (-> (stream/descriptor h)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   161\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                (assoc :dao.stream.remote/id id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   162\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                       :dao.stream/identity identity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   163\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                       :dao.stream.remote/surface (:surface entry))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   164\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (if-not (contains? (into #{} (:surface entry))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   165\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                             (required-surface op))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   166\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (write-answer! chan-writer\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   167\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                           (error-answer identity id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   168\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                         :dao.stream.remote/no-surface))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   169\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (let [ctx {:dao.stream.remote/channel channel}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   170\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                  outcome (middleware/apply-request h ctx req)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   171\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                  more (when (and (= :dao.stream/next op)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   172\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                  (valid-budget? req)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   173\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                  (= :dao.stream/ok\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   174\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                     (:dao.stream/outcome outcome)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   175\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                         (chase h ctx (:dao.stream.remote/budget req)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   176\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                outcome))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   177\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                  answer (cond-> (assoc outcome\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   178\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                        :dao.stream.remote/id id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   179\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                        :dao.stream/identity identity)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   180\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                           (seq more) (assoc :dao.stream.remote/more\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   181\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                             more))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   182\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t              (write-answer! chan-writer answer))))))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   183\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   184\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   185\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn mirror-step\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   186\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The pure step a peer runs over a channel to answer requests against\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   187\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   its table: `(mirror-step table chan-reader cursor chan-writer) ->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   188\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   cursor'`. For each request read from chan-reader at `cursor`, in\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   189\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   order, the four steps of 2.3 run; the mirror holds no state between\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   190\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   calls beyond the returned cursor. A value that is neither a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   191\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   well-formed request nor a well-formed answer is dropped as malformed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   192\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   wire input. The step stops when the channel reader answers blocked\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   193\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   or end; a gap adopts the reader's own recovery cursor, the lost wire\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   194\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   values being lost. The mirror never constructs, parses or rewrites\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   195\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   a cursor, an anchor or an outcome: the served stream is the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   196\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   original, its cursors, its positions, its gap, its end.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   197\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [table chan-reader cursor chan-writer]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   198\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (let [channel (:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor chan-reader))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   199\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (loop [cursor cursor]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   200\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (let [r (stream/next chan-reader cursor)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   201\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t        (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   202\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          :dao.stream/ok\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   203\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (do (when (well-formed-request? (:dao.stream/value r))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   204\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                (answer! table chan-writer channel\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   205\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                         (:dao.stream/value r)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   206\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t              (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   207\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          :dao.stream/blocked cursor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   208\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          :dao.stream/end cursor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   209\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          :dao.stream/gap (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   210\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          cursor)))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   211\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   212\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   213\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   214\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t;; The link (2.4, 2.5)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   215\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   216\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   217\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- new-link\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   218\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"One link per channel descriptor, shared by every reflection through\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   219\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   that channel. A link holds the channel writer; the channel reader\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   220\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   and the link's own cursor on it; the outstanding request ids with\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   221\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   the request each was sent for; filed answers keyed by id; the more\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   222\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   outcomes installed at their served identity and the cursor that\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   223\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   precedes each; an optional event writer; and the policy data -- the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   224\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   resend-after k and the budget k stamped on next requests, both\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   225\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   composition data.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   226\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [chan policy]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   227\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (atom {:reader (:reader chan)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   228\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t         :writer (:writer chan)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   229\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t         :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   230\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                   (stream/cursor (:reader chan) :dao.stream/oldest))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   231\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t         :outstanding {}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   232\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t         :filed {}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   233\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t         :filed-cursors {}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   234\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t         :events (:dao.stream.remote/events policy)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   235\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t         :resend-after (:dao.stream.remote/resend-after policy)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   236\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t         :budget (:dao.stream.remote/budget policy)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   237\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t         :next-id 0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   238\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t         :channel-gone? false}))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   239\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   240\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   241\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- mint-id!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   242\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The next asker-minted id, unique per channel.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   243\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   244\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (let [n (:next-id @link)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   245\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (swap! link assoc :next-id (inc n))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   246\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    n))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   247\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   248\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   249\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- emit!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   250\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Append one event to the link's event writer when one is composed;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   251\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   without an event writer the event is dropped.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   252\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link v]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   253\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (when-some [w (:events @link)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   254\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (stream/append! w v)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   255\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   256\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   257\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- register!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   258\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Record `req` as outstanding under its id, with the request it was\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   259\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   sent for, its ask count, and the reflection that sent it.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   260\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link refl req]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   261\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (let [id (:dao.stream.remote/id req)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   262\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (swap! link assoc-in [:outstanding id]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   263\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t           {:req req :asks 0 :reflection refl})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   264\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (swap! refl update :ids conj id)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   265\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   266\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   267\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- wire-request\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   268\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"One request map for the channel, its id asker-minted; a next\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   269\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   request carries the link's budget when one is composed.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   270\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link refl op args]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   271\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (cond-> {:dao.stream/identity (:identity @refl)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   272\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t           :dao.stream.remote/op op\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   273\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t           :dao.stream.remote/args args\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   274\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t           :dao.stream.remote/id (mint-id! link)}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   275\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (and (= :dao.stream/next op) (some? (:budget @link)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   276\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (assoc :dao.stream.remote/budget (:budget @link))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   277\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   278\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   279\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- send-request!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   280\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Append one request map to the channel writer and register it as\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   281\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   outstanding only when the writer accepted the send: a send the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   282\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   writer refuses with full leaves the request unsent and nothing\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   283\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   outstanding, so the operation answers as though unanswered and the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   284\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   next ask sends again. Returns the writer's outcome.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   285\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link refl req]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   286\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (let [r (stream/append! (:writer @link) req)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   287\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   288\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (register! link refl req))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   289\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    r))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   290\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   291\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   292\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- count-ask!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   293\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Count one further ask of the outstanding request `id`; on reaching\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   294\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   the link's resend-after k, re-send it once -- the same id, a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   295\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   duplicate of an idempotent operation, which recomputes the same or a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   296\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   later, equally true answer -- and start counting afresh. append! is\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   297\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   never re-sent: it never stays outstanding beyond its send.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   298\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link id]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   299\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   300\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (let [k (:resend-after @link)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   301\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          asks (inc (:asks entry))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   302\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (swap! link assoc-in [:outstanding id :asks] asks)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   303\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (when (and (integer? k) (pos? k) (<= k asks))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   304\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t        (stream/append! (:writer @link) (:req entry))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   305\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t        (swap! link assoc-in [:outstanding id :asks] 0)))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   306\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   307\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   308\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- outstanding-for\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   309\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The id of the link's outstanding request for `op` with `arg` sent by\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   310\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   `refl`, if any; the request each outstanding id was sent for makes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   311\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   the correlation.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   312\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link refl op arg]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   313\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (when-some [[id _]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   314\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t              (first\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   315\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                (filter (fn [[_ e]]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   316\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                          (let [r (:req e)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   317\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                            (and (= refl (:reflection e))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   318\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                 (= op (:dao.stream.remote/op r))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   319\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                 (= arg (first\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   320\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                          (:dao.stream.remote/args r))))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   321\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                        (:outstanding @link)))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   322\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    id))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   323\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   324\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   325\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- filed-for\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   326\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The first filed answer for `op` with `arg` sent by `refl`, in id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   327\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   order, as [id entry]. A filed answer keeps the request it was sent\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   328\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   for and the reflection that sent it -- an answer belongs to the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   329\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   operation that caused it -- so it is found whether or not its\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   330\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   outstanding id was abandoned.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   331\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link refl op arg]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   332\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (let [filed (:filed @link)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   333\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (when-some [id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   334\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                (first\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   335\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                  (filter (fn [i]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   336\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                            (let [e (get filed i)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   337\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                  r (:req e)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   338\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                              (and (= refl (:reflection e))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   339\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                   (= op (:dao.stream.remote/op r))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   340\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                   (= arg (first\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   341\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                                            (:dao.stream.remote/args r))))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   342\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                          (sort (keys filed))))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   343\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      [id (get filed id)])))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   344\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   345\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   346\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- bare-outcome\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   347\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The source's own outcome map, verbatim: the correlation keys the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   348\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   answer envelope added are removed, nothing else.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   349\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [ans]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   350\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (dissoc ans :dao.stream.remote/id :dao.stream/identity))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   351\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   352\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   353\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- translated\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   354\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A filed protocol error at the reflection: transport-error with the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   355\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   error's name as the reason. not-found marks the reflection gone at\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   356\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   filing; no-surface and oversize mark nothing.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   357\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [e]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   358\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   359\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   :dao.stream.remote/reason e})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   360\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   361\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   362\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- learn!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   363\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The attach probe's ok: record the source's descriptor and declared\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   364\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   surface, plus :closable.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   365\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [refl answer]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   366\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (swap! refl assoc\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   367\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t         :source-descriptor (:dao.stream/descriptor answer)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   368\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t         :surface (conj (into #{} (:dao.stream.remote/surface answer))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   369\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                        :closable)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   370\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   371\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   372\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- install-more!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   373\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Install each more outcome under the answer's served identity and at\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   374\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   the cursor that precedes it, so a later next at that cursor by a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   375\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   reflection of the same stream returns the source's own outcome\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   376\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   without a request. The identity is half of the key: two served\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   377\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   identities can carry equal cursor values, and an outcome belongs to\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   378\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   its own stream.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   379\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link answer]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   380\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (let [identity (:dao.stream/identity answer)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   381\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (loop [cur (:dao.stream/cursor answer)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   382\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t           more (:dao.stream.remote/more answer)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   383\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (when (and cur (seq more))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   384\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t        (let [[o & further] more]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   385\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (swap! link assoc-in [:filed-cursors [identity cur]] o)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   386\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (recur (:dao.stream/cursor o) further))))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   387\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   388\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   389\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- absorb!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   390\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Consume one value read off the channel. A well-formed answer whose\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   391\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   id is outstanding is taken: a not-found error marks the reflection\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   392\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   gone; the attach probe's ok records the source's descriptor and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   393\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   declared surface; an append!'s source outcome is emitted on the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   394\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   event writer, correlated by id; any other answer is filed under its\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   395\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   id and its more outcomes installed. Answers whose id is not\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   396\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   outstanding, and values that are not well-formed answers, are\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   397\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   dropped as diagnostics.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   398\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link v]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   399\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (when (well-formed-answer? v)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   400\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (let [id (:dao.stream.remote/id v)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   401\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   402\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t        (let [refl (:reflection entry)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   403\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t              req (:req entry)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   404\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t              op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   405\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t              e (:dao.stream.remote/error v)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   406\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (swap! link update :outstanding dissoc id)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   407\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (swap! refl update :ids disj id)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   408\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (cond\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   409\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (= :dao.stream.remote/not-found e)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   410\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (do (swap! refl assoc :gone? true)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   411\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                (when (or (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   412\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                          (= :dao.stream/append! op))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   413\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                  (emit! link v)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   414\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   415\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   416\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            ;; The attach probe's confirmation. ok records; a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   417\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            ;; no-surface or oversize error marks nothing.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   418\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (when (nil? e)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   419\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t              (learn! refl v)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   420\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t              (emit! link v))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   421\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   422\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (= :dao.stream/append! op)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   423\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (emit! link v)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   424\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   425\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            :else\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   426\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (do (swap! link assoc-in\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   427\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                       [:filed id] {:req req :ans v :reflection refl})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   428\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                (install-more! link v))))))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   429\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   430\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   431\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- channel-loss!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   432\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The channel reader answered end: the channel is gone. The link\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   433\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   abandons its outstanding ids, reporting each abandoned append! on\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   434\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   the event writer as append-unknown; filed answers are kept and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   435\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   still returned; reattachment is the caller's policy.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   436\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   437\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (doseq [[id entry] (:outstanding @link)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   438\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (when (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req entry)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   439\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (emit! link {:dao.stream.remote/event\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   440\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                   :dao.stream.remote/append-unknown\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   441\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                   :dao.stream.remote/id id}))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   442\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (swap! (:reflection entry) update :ids disj id))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   443\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (swap! link assoc :outstanding {} :channel-gone? true))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   444\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   445\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   446\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- drain!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   447\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Read the link's channel reader to blocked, filing each answer: the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   448\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   caller's own polling is the cadence and no driver step exists. An\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   449\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   end is the channel's loss; a gap adopts the reader's own recovery\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   450\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   cursor, the lost wire values being lost. Each drain is also one\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   451\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   further ask of an outstanding descriptor probe -- the probe's\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   452\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   caller never asks it remotely -- so resend-after re-sends it.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   453\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   454\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   455\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (doseq [[_ e] (:outstanding @link)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   456\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (when (= :dao.stream/descriptor (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req e)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   457\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t        (count-ask! link (:dao.stream.remote/id (:req e)))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   458\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (loop []\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   459\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (let [r (stream/next (:reader @link) (:cursor @link))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   460\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t        (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   461\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          :dao.stream/ok\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   462\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (do (absorb! link (:dao.stream/value r))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   463\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t              (swap! link assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   464\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t              (recur))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   465\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          :dao.stream/blocked nil\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   466\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          :dao.stream/end (channel-loss! link)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   467\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          :dao.stream/gap\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   468\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (do (swap! link assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r)) nil)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   469\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          nil)))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   470\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   471\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   472\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   473\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t;; The reflection (2.4)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   474\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   475\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   476\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- result\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   477\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [outcome]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   478\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  {:dao.stream/outcome outcome})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   479\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   480\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   481\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- refl-descriptor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   482\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Local: ok with the remote descriptor the reflection was attached\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   483\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   with and the identity -- the same identity as the source's own\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   484\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   descriptor, different reachability. A name outlives what it named:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   485\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   descriptor still answers ok once gone, once closed, and after\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   486\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   channel loss.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   487\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [refl]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   488\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (drain! (:link @refl))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   489\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   490\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   :dao.stream/descriptor (:descriptor @refl)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   491\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   :dao.stream/identity (:identity @refl)})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   492\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   493\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   494\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- surface-lacks?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   495\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"True when the source's declared surface is learned and lacks the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   496\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   surface `op` needs. Before the probe's answer the reflection\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   497\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   declares #{:reader :writer :closable}, so every operation is\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   498\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   attempted; an operation the source turns out to lack is answered as\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   499\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   the no-surface case.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   500\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [refl op]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   501\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (let [s (:surface @refl)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   502\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (and (some? s) (not (contains? s (required-surface op))))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   503\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   504\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   505\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- filed-answer-outcome\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   506\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The outcome a filed answer yields: a protocol error translated per\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   507\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   the rules, otherwise the source's outcome map verbatim.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   508\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [ans]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   509\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (or (some-> (:dao.stream.remote/error ans) translated)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   510\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (bare-outcome ans)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   511\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   512\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   513\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- filed-cursor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   514\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A filed answer for anchor `a` sent by `refl`, returned without\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   515\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   being forgotten: minting is idempotent, so the answer stays as true\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   516\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   as when it was minted.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   517\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link refl a]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   518\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (when-some [[_ entry] (filed-for link refl :dao.stream/cursor a)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   519\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (filed-answer-outcome (:ans entry))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   520\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   521\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   522\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- filed-next!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   523\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A filed answer for cursor `c` sent by `refl`: the outcome an\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   524\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   installed more element put at `c` for the stream `refl` serves,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   525\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   else the filed answer of a next request for `c`; returned and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   526\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   forgotten.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   527\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link refl c]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   528\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (let [k [(:identity @refl) c]]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   529\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (or (when-some [o (get (:filed-cursors @link) k)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   530\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (swap! link update :filed-cursors dissoc k)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   531\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (filed-answer-outcome o))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   532\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t        (when-some [[id entry]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   533\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                    (filed-for link refl :dao.stream/next c)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   534\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (swap! link update :filed dissoc id)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   535\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (filed-answer-outcome (:ans entry))))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   536\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   537\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   538\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- retry-read\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   539\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The answer a just-sent cursor request gives: the source's map,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   540\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   invalid-anchor included, arrives later as an answer.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   541\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  []\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   542\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   543\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   :dao.stream/retry? true})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   544\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   545\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   546\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- send-or-count!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   547\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Send the request for `op` with `arg` when none of this reflection's\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   548\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   own is outstanding; otherwise count one further ask of the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   549\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   outstanding request, which re-sends it at the link's resend-after\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   550\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   k.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   551\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link refl op arg]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   552\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (if-some [id (outstanding-for link refl op arg)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   553\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (count-ask! link id)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   554\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (send-request! link refl (wire-request link refl op [arg]))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   555\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   556\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   557\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- refl-cursor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   558\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The cursor operation: a filed answer for the anchor is returned,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   559\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   and a filed protocol error translated; otherwise a cursor request\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   560\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   is sent if none is outstanding, and the answer is transport-error\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   561\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   with :dao.stream/retry? true. Once closed, cursor answers closed;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   562\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   once gone, transport-error naming not-found.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   563\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [refl a]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   564\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (let [link (:link @refl)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   565\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (drain! link)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   566\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (cond\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   567\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (:closed? @refl) (result :dao.stream/closed)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   568\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (:gone? @refl) (translated :dao.stream.remote/not-found)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   569\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (surface-lacks? refl :dao.stream/cursor)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   570\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (translated :dao.stream.remote/no-surface)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   571\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      :else\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   572\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (or (filed-cursor link refl a)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   573\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   574\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (send-or-count! link refl :dao.stream/cursor a)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   575\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (retry-read))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   576\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (translated :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone)))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   577\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   578\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   579\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- refl-next\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   580\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The next operation: a filed answer for the cursor is returned and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   581\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   forgotten; otherwise a next request is sent if none is outstanding,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   582\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   and the answer is blocked -- nothing is observable at this position\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   583\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   through this handle yet. After close, filed outcomes then end. The\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   584\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   reflection never judges a cursor: cursor-mismatch and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   585\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   invalid-cursor are only ever relayed from the source.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   586\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [refl c]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   587\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (let [link (:link @refl)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   588\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (drain! link)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   589\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (cond\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   590\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (:closed? @refl)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   591\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (or (filed-next! link refl c) (result :dao.stream/end))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   592\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   593\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (:gone? @refl) (translated :dao.stream.remote/not-found)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   594\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   595\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (surface-lacks? refl :dao.stream/next)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   596\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (translated :dao.stream.remote/no-surface)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   597\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   598\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      :else\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   599\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (or (filed-next! link refl c)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   600\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   601\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (send-or-count! link refl :dao.stream/next c)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   602\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (result :dao.stream/blocked))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   603\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (translated :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone)))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   604\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   605\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   606\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- refl-append\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   607\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The append! operation: send the request and return the channel\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   608\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   writer's outcome -- ok is acceptance on the outbound path, exactly\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   609\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   the contract's Writing rule for a transport that carries values\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   610\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   toward a stream elsewhere. The source's outcome is emitted on the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   611\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   event writer when it is filed, correlated by id; append! never\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   612\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   answers the source's full. Only an accepted send is in flight: a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   613\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   refused append! never crossed, so its effect is not unknown.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   614\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [refl v]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   615\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (let [link (:link @refl)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   616\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (drain! link)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   617\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (cond\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   618\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (:closed? @refl) (result :dao.stream/closed)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   619\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (:gone? @refl) (translated :dao.stream.remote/not-found)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   620\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (surface-lacks? refl :dao.stream/append!)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}\\\\\\\\n./collab/1790479176072-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice2-confirm.gpt-6-sol.stdout.log:16:{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item_7\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1790476861675-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice2-gate.gpt-6-sol.findings.md collab/1790476870000-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice2-fixes.glm-flash.report.md'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-27 02:41:46 GMT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-27 09:41:46 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nP1 | [remote.cljc:278](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc:278) | `send-request!` registers a `descriptor`, `cursor`, or `next` request even when the channel writer refuses it with `full`. Later calls find that unsent request outstanding ([line 543](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc:543)); with no `resend-after`, they never send it. A transient full channel can therefore strand the attach probe or a read indefinitely. | Register only accepted sends, or retry a refused send on the next ask.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nP1 | [remote.cljc:374](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc:374) | Budget chase outcomes are keyed only by cursor and consumed by any reflection on the shared link ([line 520](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc:520)). Two served identities can use equal cursor values, letting a `next` on one reflection return the other stream’s outcome. | Key installed outcomes by served identity and cursor, while retaining sharing among reflections of the same stream.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nOf the ten reported readings, channel context, budget minting, whole-answer oversize, reader gap recovery, probe resend cadence, append event handling, stated precedence, correlation-key stripping, and protocol implementation are acceptable readings on inspection. Filing by reflection and operation is acceptable for direct answers; the shared `:more` filing has the cross-identity defect above. The mirror’s dispatch order and middleware path match §2.3, and I found no privileged server or client role. The orchestrator’s JVM, Node, and Dart results are accepted as supplied; I did not rerun suites.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nSign-off: DENIEDBoth P1 findings fixed; only the two permitted files touched; gate-confirmed behavior preserved (nine ratified readings, mirror dispatch order, no privilege roles — all pre-existing tests unchanged and green).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Fix 1 — refused send no longer registered (P1, remote.cljc:278)**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc:278-289`: `send-request!` now calls `register!` only when the writer answered `:dao.stream/ok`. A send refused with `full` leaves the request unsent and nothing outstanding, so `outstanding-for` (remote.cljc:549) does not strand the next ask — the retry cases re-send on the next ask, exactly per 2.4's \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"leaves the request unsent and the operation answers as though unanswered\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". This covers the attach probe (remote.cljc:823) and cursor/next sends; `refl-append` (remote.cljc:620-628) already registered only accepted appends and is untouched.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Fix 2 — installed outcomes keyed by served identity AND cursor (P1, remote.cljc:374)**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- `remote.cljc:369-387` `install-more!`: installs each more outcome under `[:filed-cursors [identity cur]]`, with `identity` taken from the answer envelope — reflections of the same stream share the same key, so sharing on the link is retained.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- `remote.cljc:524-534` `filed-next!`: consumes the installed outcome at `[(:identity @refl) c]`; a next on one identity can no longer return another stream's outcome at an equal cursor.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- `remote.cljc:217-226`: `new-link` docstring updated to state the identity+cursor keying. No other consumer of `:filed-cursors` exists.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Tests added** (`/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/dao/stream/remote_test.cljc`)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Helper `full-then-forward-writer` (:148): a writer refusing the first n appends with `:dao.stream/full`, then forwarding.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Helper `list-stream` (:163): a minimal served reader whose cursors are bare positions, so two served identities can hold equal cursor values (ringbuffer cursors embed a random-uuid identity and can never be `=`).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- `a-full-refused-send-leaves-nothing-outstanding` (:583): attach and first read pass through a refusing writer; the read answers unanswered-style (`transport-error` + `retry?`), nothing crosses; when the writer recovers the very next ask sends (1 cursor request on the wire — 0 under the old code, which strands the outstanding entry), and after one `serve!` the following ask returns the source's own cursor outcome.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- `installed-outcomes-stay-with-their-own-stream` (:488): two identities \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"p\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"q\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" on one link, equal cursor values asserted; each reflection's next returns only its own stream's outcomes (`:a1/:a2` vs `:b1/:b2`); a third reflection of \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"p\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" shares p's installed outcome without a request, and q's installed outcome is untouched.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- ns docstring extended with the two new proofs.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Bite check: with both fixes temporarily reverted, exactly these two tests fail (6 assertions); all 18 pre-existing tests pass. Fixed file restored from /tmp; no git state operations used.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Lane verification (sequential, solo, exact counts)**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- JVM `mise exec -- clojure -M:test`: Ran 2,254 tests containing 183,208 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors. (baseline 2,252/183,193/0; +2/+15)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Node `mise exec -- bb test:cljs`: Ran 2,166 tests containing 49,814 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors. (baseline 2,164/49,799/0; +2/+15)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Dart `mise exec -- bb test:cljd`: All tests passed! — 2,128 passed. (baseline 2,126; +2; new tests verified present in the fresh `test/cljd-out/dao/stream/remote-test_test.dart`)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nHygiene: `cljstyle check` clean on both files; `clj-kondo` 0 errors, 0 warnings; pure ASCII; no line over 80 columns; no leftover diagnostics; no tracked file modified and no commit/stage/checkout/reset/stash performed.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nStatus: COMPLETE\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}\\\\\\\\n./collab/1790479176072-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice2-confirm.gpt-6-sol.stdout.log:18:{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item_8\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc | sed -n '389,855p'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"   389\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- absorb!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   390\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Consume one value read off the channel. A well-formed answer whose\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   391\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   id is outstanding is taken: a not-found error marks the reflection\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   392\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   gone; the attach probe's ok records the source's descriptor and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   393\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   declared surface; an append!'s source outcome is emitted on the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   394\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   event writer, correlated by id; any other answer is filed under its\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   395\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   id and its more outcomes installed. Answers whose id is not\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   396\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   outstanding, and values that are not well-formed answers, are\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   397\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   dropped as diagnostics.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   398\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link v]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   399\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (when (well-formed-answer? v)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   400\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (let [id (:dao.stream.remote/id v)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   401\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   402\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t        (let [refl (:reflection entry)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   403\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t              req (:req entry)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   404\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t              op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   405\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t              e (:dao.stream.remote/error v)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   406\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (swap! link update :outstanding dissoc id)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   407\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (swap! refl update :ids disj id)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   408\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (cond\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   409\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (= :dao.stream.remote/not-found e)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   410\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (do (swap! refl assoc :gone? true)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   411\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                (when (or (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   412\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                          (= :dao.stream/append! op))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   413\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                  (emit! link v)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   414\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   415\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   416\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            ;; The attach probe's confirmation. ok records; a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   417\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            ;; no-surface or oversize error marks nothing.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   418\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (when (nil? e)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   419\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t              (learn! refl v)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   420\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t              (emit! link v))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   421\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   422\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (= :dao.stream/append! op)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   423\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (emit! link v)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   424\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   425\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            :else\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   426\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t            (do (swap! link assoc-in\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   427\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                       [:filed id] {:req req :ans v :reflection refl})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   428\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                (install-more! link v))))))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   429\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   430\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   431\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- channel-loss!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   432\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The channel reader answered end: the channel is gone. The link\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   433\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   abandons its outstanding ids, reporting each abandoned append! on\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   434\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   the event writer as append-unknown; filed answers are kept and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   435\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   still returned; reattachment is the caller's policy.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   436\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   437\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (doseq [[id entry] (:outstanding @link)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   438\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (when (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req entry)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   439\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (emit! link {:dao.stream.remote/event\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   440\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                   :dao.stream.remote/append-unknown\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   441\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                   :dao.stream.remote/id id}))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   442\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (swap! (:reflection entry) update :ids disj id))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   443\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (swap! link assoc :outstanding {} :channel-gone? true))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   444\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   445\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   446\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- drain!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   447\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Read the link's channel reader to blocked, filing each answer: the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   448\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   caller's own polling is the cadence and no driver step exists. An\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   449\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   end is the channel's loss; a gap adopts the reader's own recovery\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   450\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   cursor, the lost wire values being lost. Each drain is also one\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   451\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   further ask of an outstanding descriptor probe -- the probe's\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   452\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   caller never asks it remotely -- so resend-after re-sends it.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   453\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   454\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   455\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (doseq [[_ e] (:outstanding @link)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   456\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (when (= :dao.stream/descriptor (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req e)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   457\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t        (count-ask! link (:dao.stream.remote/id (:req e)))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   458\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (loop []\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   459\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (let [r (stream/next (:reader @link) (:cursor @link))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   460\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t        (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   461\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          :dao.stream/ok\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   462\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (do (absorb! link (:dao.stream/value r))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   463\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t              (swap! link assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   464\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t              (recur))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   465\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          :dao.stream/blocked nil\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   466\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          :dao.stream/end (channel-loss! link)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   467\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          :dao.stream/gap\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   468\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (do (swap! link assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r)) nil)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   469\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          nil)))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   470\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   471\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   472\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   473\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t;; The reflection (2.4)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   474\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   475\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   476\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- result\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   477\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [outcome]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   478\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  {:dao.stream/outcome outcome})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   479\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   480\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   481\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- refl-descriptor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   482\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Local: ok with the remote descriptor the reflection was attached\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   483\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   with and the identity -- the same identity as the source's own\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   484\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   descriptor, different reachability. A name outlives what it named:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   485\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   descriptor still answers ok once gone, once closed, and after\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   486\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   channel loss.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   487\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [refl]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   488\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (drain! (:link @refl))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   489\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   490\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   :dao.stream/descriptor (:descriptor @refl)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   491\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   :dao.stream/identity (:identity @refl)})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   492\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   493\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   494\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- surface-lacks?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   495\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"True when the source's declared surface is learned and lacks the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   496\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   surface `op` needs. Before the probe's answer the reflection\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   497\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   declares #{:reader :writer :closable}, so every operation is\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   498\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   attempted; an operation the source turns out to lack is answered as\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   499\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   the no-surface case.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   500\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [refl op]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   501\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (let [s (:surface @refl)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   502\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (and (some? s) (not (contains? s (required-surface op))))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   503\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   504\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   505\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- filed-answer-outcome\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   506\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The outcome a filed answer yields: a protocol error translated per\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   507\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   the rules, otherwise the source's outcome map verbatim.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   508\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [ans]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   509\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (or (some-> (:dao.stream.remote/error ans) translated)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   510\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t      (bare-outcome ans)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   511\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   512\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   513\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- filed-cursor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   514\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A filed answer for anchor `a` sent by `refl`, returned without\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   515\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   being forgotten: minting is idempotent, so the answer stays as true\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   516\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   as when it was minted.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   517\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link refl a]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   518\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (when-some [[_ entry] (filed-for link refl :dao.stream/cursor a)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   519\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (filed-answer-outcome (:ans entry))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   520\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   521\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   522\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- filed-next!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   523\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A filed answer for cursor `c` sent by `refl`: the outcome an\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   524\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   installed more element put at `c` for the stream `refl` serves,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   525\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   else the filed answer of a next request for `c`; returned and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   526\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   forgotten.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   527\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link refl c]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   528\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  (let [k [(:identity @refl) c]]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   529\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t    (or (when-some [o (get (:filed-cursors @link) k)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   530\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (swap! link update :filed-cursors dissoc k)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   531\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (filed-answer-outcome o))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   532\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t        (when-some [[id entry]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   533\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t                    (filed-for link refl :dao.stream/next c)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   534\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (swap! link update :filed dissoc id)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   535\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t          (filed-answer-outcome (:ans entry))))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   536\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   537\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   538\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- retry-read\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   539\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The answer a just-sent cursor request gives: the source's map,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   540\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   invalid-anchor included, arrives later as an answer.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   541\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  []\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   542\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   543\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   :dao.stream/retry? true})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   544\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   545\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   546\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t(defn- send-or-count!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   547\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Send the request for `op` with `arg` when none of this reflection's\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   548\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   own is outstanding; otherwise count one further ask of the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   549\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   outstanding request, which re-sends it at the link's resend-after\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   550\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t   k.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   551\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\t  [link refl op arg]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   55