{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/dao-stream/1794149009000-engineer-step1-remediation.muse-wonder-1.0.stdout.log; nl -ba docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md | sed -n '446,486p'; nl -ba test/yin/repl/store_test.cljc | sed -n '1540,1630p'\"","aggregated_output":"muse: workspace root: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht (cwd default)\nmuse: workspace trust: trusted source=run-flag\nmuse: warning: rules file at /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/CLAUDE.md is ignored this session because AGENTS.md takes precedence in that directory; merge still-applicable guidance into AGENTS.md or remove one of the two files\nmuse: Skills: 38 loaded · 1 warning\nmuse:   `skills_catalog` was trimmed to fit its size limit (32 KB): 1 descriptions compacted, 0 skill ids omitted\nmuse:   Run `muse skills list --source all` for full diagnostics.\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-08 15:04:55 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-08 22:04:55 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nStep 1 remediation is complete. All three architect findings are addressed. Changes this session touch only [fixture.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/test/yin/repl/fixture.cljc) and [index_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc) on branch `yin-repl-dht-composition` at HEAD `b88bad9dd93d233f1d78e5a111444f6c8d86c9aa`. `src/` is untouched. The pre-existing Step 1 edits in query, require, and store tests were not modified this session.\n\n**Finding 1 — publication-result protocol.** The fixture now records each HEAD call as one explicit section 4 result after its outcome is known, with `:op`, minted `:id`/`:round`, `:manifest`, `:status`, and local `:durability`. A refusal can no longer look like a success. [fixture.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/test/yin/repl/fixture.cljc) adds `publication-request`, `publication-result`, `publication-result-expectations`, and the test-local `accept-result` model. The expectations cover matching success, refusal, delayed completion, wrong id, wrong round, wrong manifest, duplicate, and stale delivery. Synchronous pins now assert the explicit records. The new oracle test pins the six undeliverable cases against the model and labels them Step 2 oracle, distinct from the synchronous pins.\n\n**Finding 3 — shell retry defect.** The new shell acceptance test asserts the correct retry behavior and currently fails. Its comment records the baseline revision, test identifier, command, and signature. The narrower indexer oracle stays green. The engine fix stays deferred to Step 2. A probe first reproduced the defect on both backends: the retry answered the `(name nil)` error text and rolled back.\n\n**Finding 2 — invariant evidence.** Every run used `clojure -M:test -n <ns> -v <ns>/<var>` at the recorded revision. The slow cadence run also set `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1`. Full logs are in the [evidence directory](/tmp/step1-evidence/) with the [revision record](/tmp/step1-evidence/revision.txt).\n\n| §8 pin | Focused tests | JVM outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| Frontier gate | frontier agreement, stale cursor, suffix, settle-once | green, 54/42/8/16 assertions |\n| Restore Settings | recovery cursors, allocator watermark, F2 refault, restore refusals, restart restore | green, 12/8/4/5/13 assertions |\n| Repair cadence | two-peer ack, prompt retry, twenty-round ticker idle | green, 6/3/25 assertions |\n| Cross-host parity | incremental vs full, root replay, backend swap | green, 84/4/13 assertions |\n| Lifecycle baseline | hydration gate, bind refusal, heads write order, close once, parked-once, rollback answers | green, 8/4/6/6/8/7/24 assertions |\n\nNamespace checkpoints confirm isolation. Index runs 29 tests and 629 assertions with 11 failures and 0 errors. All 11 failures sit inside the single known shell-retry test. Store runs 28/145 green, query 18/279 green, and require 20/209 green. Kondo reports 0 errors and 0 warnings on both edited files.\n\nSection 11 classification is narrow. The shell-retry failure is a known boundary failure with a matched signature, owned by the Step 2 `notice` fix. The JVM ticker-idle fixture is green at this revision, so it is not a current JVM red. Node and Dart legs, the Node composition failure, and the eight-distinct acknowledgement fixture were not run under G0 and are reported unverified, not green. The section 9 boundary-neutral reds remain separately gated and do not block Step 1.\n   446\t\n   447\t## 8. Invariants to pin before relocation\n   448\t\n   449\tA partially red integration suite permits starting the refactor only\n   450\twhen failures are classified and narrower invariant tests provide a\n   451\ttrustworthy oracle. The following invariants are pinned green, at the\n   452\tnarrower level, before their implementation moves. Known failing\n   453\tend-to-end fixtures remain as failing acceptance tests until the\n   454\tcompleted refactor fixes them. If a Node compilation or composition\n   455\tfailure prevents those pins from running, that test path is restored\n   456\tfirst: absence of results is not evidence of preservation.\n   457\t\n   458\t**Frontier gate.** Manifest identity, published transaction count,\n   459\tcount-cap compatibility, cursor ownership, and expected suffix length\n   460\tmust agree. Stale, ahead, or foreign cursors reconstruct fully. Missing\n   461\tcontent or failed HEAD persistence must not advance the frontier.\n   462\tExisting fixtures include `test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc:385` and\n   463\t`test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc:421`.\n   464\t\n   465\t**Restore Settings threading.** The manifest's count cap reaches every\n   466\trestored node and recording storage. Strong session references and\n   467\tdurable refault sources remain intact. Recovery derives allocator\n   468\tauthority from history rather than saved process cursors. Byte policy\n   469\treaches the restored publisher separately.\n   470\t\n   471\t**Repair cadence.** One owner advances transport state using supplied\n   472\ttime. Fresh writes retain capacity while repairs progress; queues stay\n   473\tbounded; delayed future repairs do not imply perpetual busy status. The\n   474\ttwenty-publication/400-tick fixture's requirement for both active repair\n   475\tand subsequent idle periods is preserved.\n   476\t\n   477\t**Cross-host parity.** Identical supported inputs, publication path, and\n   478\tpolicy yield identical bytes and addresses across JVM, Node, and Dart.\n   479\tBulk and incremental paths need logical equivalence; they need not\n   480\tproduce identical tree shapes.\n   481\t\n   482\t**Lifecycle and causality.** Hydration gates input; failed bind or load\n   483\trefuses rather than starting empty; `heads.edn` persistence precedes head\n   484\tinstallation; relevant completions resume parked work once; rollback\n   485\tpreserves already-settled effects; shutdown closes resources once.\n   486\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
