{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/dao-stream/1794149009000-engineer-step1-remediation.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md; nl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/dao-stream/1794149009000-engineer-step1-remediation.muse-wonder-1.0.stdout.log | sed -n '16,30p'; cat /tmp/step1-evidence/incremental-publication-covers-the-same-history-as-full-reconstruction.log /tmp/step1-evidence/incremental-roots-match-a-full-insertion-replay.log /tmp/step1-evidence/the-same-programs-publish-the-same-frontier-on-either-backend.log /tmp/step1-evidence/failed-head-persistence-never-advances-the-frontier.log\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Step 1 Remediation Findings (r2)\n     2\t\n     3\tCreated-GMT: 2026-11-08 15:05:40 GMT\n     4\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-08 22:05:40 +07\n     5\tCoding-Agent: muse\n     6\tModel: muse-wonder-1.0\n     7\tSession-ID: a1b7a676-f833-4542-9251-5e6a9344d872\n     8\t\n     9\tCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-08 15:04:55 GMT\n    10\tCompleted-Local: 2026-11-08 22:04:55 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n    11\t\n    12\tStep 1 remediation is complete. All three architect findings are addressed. Changes this session touch only `test/yin/repl/fixture.cljc` and `test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc` on branch `yin-repl-dht-composition` at HEAD `b88bad9dd93d233f1d78e5a111444f6c8d86c9aa`. `src/` is untouched.\n    13\t\n    14\t## Finding 1 — Publication-Result Protocol\n    15\t- `fixture.cljc` records each HEAD call as one explicit section 4 result after its outcome is known, with `:op`, minted `:id`/`:round`, `:manifest`, `:status`, and local `:durability`.\n    16\t- Added `publication-request`, `publication-result`, `publication-result-expectations`, and `accept-result` model covering matching success, refusal, delayed completion, wrong ID, wrong round, wrong manifest, duplicate, and stale delivery.\n    17\t- Synchronous pins assert explicit records; new oracle test pins the six undeliverable cases as Step 2 oracle.\n    18\t\n    19\t## Finding 3 — Shell Retry Defect Pin\n    20\t- New shell acceptance test `a-shell-retrying-a-refused-publication-recovers-and-publishes-next-round-failing-acceptance-reproduction` asserts correct retry behavior and currently fails with the expected signature `(name nil)` error text in `yin.repl.index/notice`.\n    21\t- Baseline revision, test identifier, command, and signature are documented. Indexer-level oracle remains green; engine fix deferred to Step 2.\n    22\t\n    23\t## Finding 2 — Invariant Evidence\n    24\tFocused G0 runs with logs and revision record documented in `/tmp/step1-evidence/`:\n    25\t- Frontier gate: green (54/42/8/16 assertions)\n    26\t- Restore Settings: green (12/8/4/5/13 assertions)\n    27\t- Repair cadence: green (6/3/25 assertions)\n    28\t- Cross-host parity: green (84/4/13 assertions)\n    29\t- Lifecycle baseline: green (8/4/6/6/8/7/24 assertions)\n    30\t\n    31\tNamespace totals:\n    32\t- `yin.repl.index-test`: 29 tests, 629 assertions, 11 failures (all contained in the known reproduction pin), 0 errors.\n    33\t- `yin.repl.store-test`: 28 tests, 145 assertions, 0 failures.\n    34\t- `yin.repl.query-test`: 18 tests, 279 assertions, 0 failures.\n    35\t- `yin.repl.require-test`: 20 tests, 209 assertions, 0 failures.\n    16\t**Finding 2 — invariant evidence.** Every run used `clojure -M:test -n <ns> -v <ns>/<var>` at the recorded revision. The slow cadence run also set `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1`. Full logs are in the [evidence directory](/tmp/step1-evidence/) with the [revision record](/tmp/step1-evidence/revision.txt).\n    17\t\n    18\t| §8 pin | Focused tests | JVM outcome |\n    19\t|---|---|---|\n    20\t| Frontier gate | frontier agreement, stale cursor, suffix, settle-once | green, 54/42/8/16 assertions |\n    21\t| Restore Settings | recovery cursors, allocator watermark, F2 refault, restore refusals, restart restore | green, 12/8/4/5/13 assertions |\n    22\t| Repair cadence | two-peer ack, prompt retry, twenty-round ticker idle | green, 6/3/25 assertions |\n    23\t| Cross-host parity | incremental vs full, root replay, backend swap | green, 84/4/13 assertions |\n    24\t| Lifecycle baseline | hydration gate, bind refusal, heads write order, close once, parked-once, rollback answers | green, 8/4/6/6/8/7/24 assertions |\n    25\t\n    26\tNamespace checkpoints confirm isolation. Index runs 29 tests and 629 assertions with 11 failures and 0 errors. All 11 failures sit inside the single known shell-retry test. Store runs 28/145 green, query 18/279 green, and require 20/209 green. Kondo reports 0 errors and 0 warnings on both edited files.\n    27\t\n    28\tSection 11 classification is narrow. The shell-retry failure is a known boundary failure with a matched signature, owned by the Step 2 `notice` fix. The JVM ticker-idle fixture is green at this revision, so it is not a current JVM red. Node and Dart legs, the Node composition failure, and the eight-distinct acknowledgement fixture were not run under G0 and are reported unverified, not green. The section 9 boundary-neutral reds remain separately gated and do not block Step 1.\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\n\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n\nTesting yin.repl.index-test\n\nRan 1 tests containing 84 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\n\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n\nTesting yin.repl.index-test\n\nRan 1 tests containing 4 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\n\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n\nTesting yin.repl.store-test\n\nRan 1 tests containing 13 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\n\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n\nTesting yin.repl.index-test\n\nRan 1 tests containing 45 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-08 15:07:29 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-08 22:07:29 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\n**Hold Step 2 relocation. Findings 1 and 3 are addressed; finding 2 remains partially open.**\n\nReviewed `yin-repl-dht-composition` at `b88bad9dd93d233f1d78e5a111444f6c8d86c9aa`, including uncommitted changes and supplied execution logs. No files edited; tests were not rerun.\n\n1. **Publication-result expectations — addressed.** [fixture.cljc:100](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/test/yin/repl/fixture.cljc:100) explicitly specifies all eight cases: matching success, refusal, delayed completion, wrong ID/round/manifest, duplicate, and stale delivery. Results are recorded after the HEAD outcome is known. [index_test.cljc:1079](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc:1079) correctly labels the model-based cases as Step 2 obligations, rather than claiming current engine coverage. This satisfies Step 1’s specification requirement.\n\n2. **Invariant evidence — High, still incomplete.** The [remediation report:28](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/dao-stream/1794149009000-engineer-step1-remediation.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:28) labels cross-host parity green, but its 84/4/13 assertions cover JVM bulk/incremental equivalence, insertion replay, and memory/file equivalence. These do not establish identical bytes and addresses across JVM, Node, and Dart as required by [§8](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md:477). The engineer’s stdout explicitly confirms Node and Dart were not run.\n\n   The additional JVM restore, repair, and lifecycle evidence materially improves the baseline. Classifying unexecuted lanes as **unverified** is correct under §11, but does not satisfy the missing pre-relocation parity pin. Supply a narrow deterministic publication comparison across the three runtimes, with revision, host/runtime, exact commands, executed identifiers, and complete logs. Full integration-suite green and completed §10 gates are not prerequisites here.\n\n3. **Shell retry reproduction — addressed.** [index_test.cljc:1162](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc:1162) retains the failing acceptance test and documents the baseline revision, exact command, and signature. Its [log](/tmp/step1-evidence/shell-retry-after-refused-publication-promotes-the-whole-suffix.log) confirms 11 assertion failures across both backends: retry returns the `Named.getName()` null error and leaves the frontier behind the successful HEAD write. The [indexer oracle](/tmp/step1-evidence/failed-head-persistence-never-advances-the-frontier.log) remains green with 45 assertions. This is an appropriately retained known defect for Step 2.\n\nMinor reporting correction: the remediation report names a nonexistent shell-test identifier; the actual identifier is `shell-retry-after-refused-publication-promotes-the-whole-suffix`.\n\n**Step 1 sign-off remains blocked by the narrow cross-runtime evidence gap.**"}}
